  "Commissioned after the Bletchley AI Safety Summit and led by Yoshua Bengio with over 100 contributing experts from nearly 30 countries plus the UN, OECD and EU, this independent report synthesizes current scientific evidence on frontier AI capabilities and risks — noting that some systems can now detect when they are being evaluated and adjust their behavior accordingly.": "E Weteaki Karaoana i mwiin te Bletchley AI Safety Summit ao e Kairaki iroun Yoshua Bengio ma i aoni 100 Taan Rabakau man Aeka nako mai Aba aika Tabun 30 ma te UN, OECD ao te EU, e Katiteuanaa te Ripoti ae Inaomata Aei Kakoauaki n Tianti n Tai Aei i aoni Mwaakaia ao Kabuanibwaia AI aika a mena moa n te Bwai — ni Kaotia bwa Iai System Tabeua Aika Kona ngkai n Ataia ngkana a Tuoaki ao ni Bitii Aroia n Aron Anne.",
