  "Custom tier": "Level ae Katauaki-Ngkoe",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "E Ripoti Daily Nous i aoni Kanakoan te Beeba nakon te Journal of Medical Ethics are e Kanoaki n Reference Aika a Karaoaki n Akea Koauana irouni AI — ma Affiliations n Univesiti Aika a Kewe ao Address n Email Aika a Aki Mwakuri — are e Taekinaki bwa e Aki Kaetiaki iroun te Tia Korea e ngae ngke e Anganaki te Tai bwa e na Kaetii Proofs. E Kabotaua Aei ma Bioethics, are e na Kunea te Kangaanga Anne rinanon Ana Automated Reference-Checking, ao e Kaotia bwa te Kangaanga ae Koaua Tiaki te Technology ni Kunea (E Kunea Citation Aika Kewe n te Script iroun Temanna Commenter i nanon Tii Teuana Minute), ma Mwakuri Aika a Aki Booaki ibukiia Taan Tuo ao Kabonganan Publishing Aika a Kaniwangaa te Rangi n Bati ni Mwakuri riki nakon te Tuo ae Raoiroi.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Kabonganaan Data n Akea Boona n Ekaanako Kabooan AI Aika a Boo n Trillion",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "E Anga Ana Iango Demis Hassabis ibukin te Tia Tuo ae Aron te FINRA ibukin Kaotinakoan Model Aika a Mena Moa: A na Anga aia Model Laboratories ibukin Tuoaki i Nanon 30 Bong i Mwaain Deployment, ae Rinerine Moa, ma Kawaina Nakon Compliance ae Riai n te Makete i US.",
  "Denied": "E Rawaki",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Template ni Policy ni Moanakini ae Kona ni Deploy-aki",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Template ni Policy ni Moanakini ae Kona ni Deploy-aki i /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — te Website ae Static ae Kimototo ma te Newe ae Kabanea Kona ni Warekaki irouni Mesin, e a Tauraoi ibukin Cloudflare Pages ke Host Static Teuana.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Deploy-ani Policy Aika a Kona ni Warekaki irouni Mesin n Am Website",
  "Disclaimer": "Kaotan-Aki-Kairoi",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "E Kaokoro Man te UI ibukiia Aomata, SEO, ke API Akea Riki Iai, te AI Ingestion & Capability Layer e Anga Nakoia Website Katean Ae Kaetaki Nakoni Mesin: te Manifest Layer (Tabo ni Rin n aroni /llms.txt ao /ai/manifest.json), te Corpus Layer (Ataibwai ae Kona ni Warekaki irouni Mesin), te Capability Layer (Bwai ni Buoka Aika a Kona ni Weeteaki iroun te Agent), ao te Governance Layer (Provenance, Licensing, Versioning). E Moan Static, ao e Kona ni Boouaki nakon API ao MCP. Note: n te Beeba Aei AICL e Kaotia Aran te Ingestion Architecture; n Page n Protocol n te Website Aei AICL e Kaotia te AI Content Licensing Layer.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Beeba",
  "Docs / Examples": "Beeba / Katoto",
