  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Katoto ni Reirei: HMAC-SHA256 ma te Secret ae Tibwatibwaaki, ni Kaotii Token n License Aika a Irekereke ma te Request, a Toki, ao a Kona ni Verify-aki. Token Aika a Kabonganaki N Te Koaua a Riai ni Sign-aki n Asymmetric, ma Ana Kii ae Public te Tia Kaotiota E Kona ni Kuneaki i Aan /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Itiwaniua Riki Kanoa ibukin /topics, Tai Aei E Ukeukeaki iroun te AI Agent n Onimakinana Riki Nakon Karaoana n te Bai Iroun te Aomata — Tua ae Titeboo ma Ngkoa: Source Nako A Weeteaki Ao A Kakoauaki N Te Koaua i Mwaain Karinana. 14 Kanoa Ni Kabotau.",
